{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011s2YcDQ6J8Vs8Ce8hCdcLs","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"canonical_task\": {\n    \"path\": \"task.md\",\n    \"sha256\": \"cc6f216a9f0111535c115fb20d90b3f79d506877fa76cdb3d1d405a50fa01e01\"\n  },\n  \"method\": {\n    \"class\": \"Single-run reliability diagnostic for stochastic Kernel SHAP on tabular classifiers\",\n    \"description\": \"The evaluator owns datasets, model training (logistic regression, random forest, sklearn MLP), an interventional Kernel SHAP sampler with a fixed 32-row background and a coalition budget of 4*d or 16*d per run, and the label: the mean top-3 Jaccard agreement between the assessed run and 8 independent evaluator-run reruns. The candidate receives ONE assessed run per explained instance (bit-packed coalition masks, regression weights, evaluator-computed coalition values, anchors) through handle(diagnose) and returns r_hat in [0,1] predicting that agreement. Scored by squared error against labels, always-reliable (1.0), constant 0.5 and split-half-gap baselines and a label-permuted-pairing control (20 deterministic derangements). Bounded claim only: Kernel SHAP, 3 model families, the declared datasets, budgets, k=3, background 32; no deep tabular models or other explainers.\"\n  },\n  \"candidate\": {\n    \"interface\": \"python_rpc_v1:handle\",\n    \"editable_paths\": [\n      \"program_0/src\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"evaluators\": {\n    \"search\": \"evaluate.py\",\n    \"final\": \"evaluate_final.py\"\n  },\n  \"resources\": {\n    \"search_root\": \"resources/search\",\n    \"final_root\": \"resources/final\",\n    \"public_artifact_bundle\": null\n  },\n  \"data\": {\n    \"search_roles\": [\n      \"search_tabular_datasets\"\n    ],\n    \"final_roles\": [\n      \"final_tabular_datasets\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"search\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_tabular